!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-bare-annotation-whose-type-is-not-void-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §6"
  description: """
    A bare annotation is shorthand for `@T:_`, so it is read against its type like a written value. `doc`
    is text, and text does not admit `_`: the bare form is for a void-typed marker such as `@deprecated`,
    and here it is a resolver error, as `@doc:_` would be.

    What the vector guards is that the bare form is checked at all. A processor that validates only a
    written value would accept the mark, and a documentation annotation would carry no documentation.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
